# Coordinator wire

Import ArtifactRules from "./artifact_rules.lg".
Import AttemptRecord from "./attempt_record.lg".
Import NodeRecord from "./node_record.lg".
Import ProblemRecord from "./problem_record.lg".
Import TrailRecord from "./trail_record.lg".
Import WorkRecord from "./work_record.lg".

What the coordinator answers a worker, and the attempt a worker posts. The
answers reuse the factory's own records, so a worker decodes a grant with the
derived `fromJson_LeaseGrant` and finds in it the `WorkUnit`, `Lease`,
`Problem`, `Statement` and `Strategy` it already knows.

## Note
The answer to a lease request. `granted` is false when no unit fits, and
`reason` says why. `secret` authenticates the worker's heartbeats and attempt on
this lease (`lease_secret.lg`). `trailDigest` is what the model reads about the
problem's past; `trailSeq` and `trailHead` are the trail's last entry, the place
the attempt's own entry chains from. `context` is what the worker must know
before it starts, such as that the statement is an excerpt to complete first.

## A LeaseGrant has:
    a granted, which is Bool.
    a reason, which is Text.
    a secret, which is Text.
    a lease, which is Option of Lease.
    a unit, which is Option of WorkUnit.
    a problem, which is Option of Problem.
    a statement, which is Option of Statement.
    a strategy, which is Option of Strategy.
    a trailDigest, which is Text.
    a trailSeq, which is Int.
    a trailHead, which is Text.
    a deadEnds, which is Int.
    a context, which is Text.

## A HeartbeatAnswer has:
    an alive, which is Bool.
    an expiresAt, which is Int.

## Note
What became of a posted attempt. `outcome` is the intake's code (`recorded`,
`awaiting_verifier`, or why it was refused); `trailSeq` and `trailHash` are the
entry as stored, which differ from the posted one when it was `resealed` onto a
newer head; `verifyUnit` and `followUnit` are the units the attempt queued.

## A AttemptReceipt has:
    an accepted, which is Bool.
    an outcome, which is Text.
    a detail, which is Text.
    an attemptId, which is Text.
    a trailSeq, which is Int.
    a trailHash, which is Text.
    a resealed, which is Bool.
    a verifyUnit, which is Text.
    a followUnit, which is Text.

## Note
A formal statement a `formalize` attempt proposes: a kernel document defining
`goalName` as a `Prop`, made by route A, B or C.

## A StatementDraft has:
    a document, which is Text.
    a goalName, which is Text.
    a route, which is Text.

## Note
A posted attempt: the lease it comes under, the attempt and its trail entry, the
files it hands over, and, for a `formalize` unit, the statement it proposes.

## A AttemptSubmission has:
    a unitId, which is Text.
    a token, which is Int.
    a holder, which is Text.
    a secret, which is Text.
    an attempt, which is Attempt.
    an entry, which is TrailEntry.
    an artifacts, which is Seq of ArtifactUpload.
    a draft, which is Option of StatementDraft.
